WEBVTT

00:02.717 --> 00:06.887
<i>Like a silent disease slowly
but surely ravaging the body,</i>

00:07.221 --> 00:11.099
<i>an evil is lurking
a midst our streets, in our Morioh,</i>

00:11.851 --> 00:14.562
<i>claiming more lives
in more unknown locations.</i>

00:18.191 --> 00:21.777
<i>What's worse, the killings
have gone completely unnoticed</i>

00:22.320 --> 00:26.240
<i>It's shocking.
It's downright chilling.</i>

00:27.075 --> 00:31.079
<i>But we have no way of
finding the killer.</i>

00:32.038 --> 00:36.538
<i>Even the number of
Stand users in Morioh is a mystery</i>

00:37.418 --> 00:41.588
<i>People aren't worried about
some silent killer…</i>

00:41.798 --> 00:45.426
<i>They're worried about
what's for dinner,</i>

00:45.593 --> 00:48.971
<i>they're blind to those happenings
outside their immediate view.</i>

00:46.219 --> 00:48.971
KAMEYU

00:49.055 --> 00:51.223
TRANSACTION NO. BANK NO.
BRANCH NO. WINDOW NO.
DEPOSIT AMOUNT BALANCE

00:54.560 --> 00:57.479
I have 285 yen to my name?!

00:57.730 --> 01:00.315
I had 20,000 yen in savings!

01:06.614 --> 01:09.825
Twelve yen?!

01:10.993 --> 01:12.828
I have no willpower!

01:13.079 --> 01:17.249
That 20,000 yen was
for those dope designer shoes…

01:17.458 --> 01:20.252
What the hell did I even buy?

01:20.878 --> 01:22.838
This is all
that crusty old fart's fault!

01:22.964 --> 01:26.926
He charged 130,000 yen worth of
baby bullshit to my freak in card!

01:27.301 --> 01:29.970
I did have the old man
pay me back the 130,000,

01:30.179 --> 01:32.681
then I got bit by
this mysterious spending bug…

01:32.765 --> 01:35.017
and my money sense
flew out the window.

01:35.810 --> 01:40.310
Maybe there's a thousand yen
somewhere that I forgot about.

01:53.161 --> 01:54.620
A roach!

01:54.829 --> 01:57.331
Guess a bank's no different
from anywhere else.

02:02.920 --> 02:04.630
A S-Stand?

02:06.090 --> 02:07.966
Got one yen.

02:14.098 --> 02:15.516
Little bastard!

02:19.228 --> 02:20.520
I-It's a Stand!

02:21.022 --> 02:23.524
We have ourselves
a new Stand on our hands!

02:43.628 --> 02:44.253
JOJO'S BIZARRE ADVENTURE
DIAMOND IS UNBREAKABLE

02:44.337 --> 02:46.464
<i>A demon's crept into
our everyday life</i>

02:46.547 --> 02:48.799
<i>It's about to take away
something precious</i>

02:48.883 --> 02:52.136
<i>Our peace has already
crumbled long ago</i>

02:52.887 --> 02:54.972
<i>So casually, so nonchalantly</i>

02:55.056 --> 02:57.391
<i>It's taken from us
before we know it</i>

02:57.475 --> 03:00.728
<i>If we want it back,
now's the chance</i>

03:00.937 --> 03:04.440
<i>With the sharpness of
the piercing arrow</i>

03:05.233 --> 03:08.653
<i>The beauty of two souls united</i>

03:08.736 --> 03:11.321
<i>Wherever you go, chase you</i>

03:11.405 --> 03:13.490
<i>Whenever, chase you</i>

03:13.574 --> 03:15.576
<i>I will chase you</i>

03:15.660 --> 03:17.286
<i>Nowhere to escape</i>

03:17.370 --> 03:19.914
<i>Start running, I will chase you</i>

03:19.997 --> 03:21.999
<i>Tomorrow, chase you</i>

03:22.083 --> 03:24.794
<i>My fists will be the one
to show you</i>

03:25.002 --> 03:29.502
<i>Tenacity decides
who will win or lose</i>

03:30.716 --> 03:35.216
<i>So I chase you</i>

03:38.641 --> 03:42.811
EPISODE 18
SHIGECHI'S HARVEST, PART 1

03:47.900 --> 03:49.776
Where the hell is he running?

03:50.820 --> 03:52.029
Another one!

03:52.113 --> 03:55.324
Damn it! What the hell are you?!

03:55.491 --> 03:58.202
I'll slaughter you!

03:59.620 --> 04:00.454
Okuyasu!

04:00.538 --> 04:02.039
Oh, Josuke!

04:02.123 --> 04:05.459
Look! An enemy Stand.
I'm gonna squash him to death!

04:06.586 --> 04:07.878
There are two of 'em!

04:08.045 --> 04:11.173
Yeah. I followed one of 'em
all the way from the bank.

04:11.465 --> 04:13.467
How'd he attack you?

04:13.551 --> 04:16.345
Well, he didn't really attack me.

04:16.470 --> 04:19.097
I was buying some Calpis Water,

04:19.390 --> 04:22.267
when suddenly he popped out from
under the vending machine.

04:22.351 --> 04:25.062
What? So you weren't attacked?

04:25.313 --> 04:27.732
You just said
you'll slaughter the little guy.

04:27.982 --> 04:30.025
The little pest startled me
so much,

04:30.109 --> 04:32.694
I spilled Calpis Water
all over my uniform.

04:32.820 --> 04:34.863
Damn it! Give me back my money!

04:35.323 --> 04:36.741
Got it!

04:36.824 --> 04:39.660
Hey, another one joined the pack…

04:39.744 --> 04:41.036
Got it!

04:41.120 --> 04:43.330
Got it. Got it.

04:43.414 --> 04:45.541
What the… What are these things?

04:45.666 --> 04:48.794
There's so many of them!
They're a little army!

04:48.878 --> 04:53.048
Okuyasu, they're like
your brother Keicho's Stand.

04:53.674 --> 04:54.424
But…

04:54.800 --> 04:59.300
The way they're completely
ignoring us is kinda eerie.

05:00.264 --> 05:01.473
Yeah…

05:09.523 --> 05:13.068
Watch out!
The user's nearby… probably.

05:13.861 --> 05:14.862
BOOM

05:25.039 --> 05:25.789
It's…

05:25.957 --> 05:27.458
It's money!

05:27.708 --> 05:29.626
You know, it did swipe a 1 yen coin

05:29.710 --> 05:31.545
from underneath the atm
at the bank.

05:31.837 --> 05:33.964
It's just a bunch of
1 yen and 10 yen coins,

05:34.048 --> 05:35.591
but they're the real deal!

05:36.300 --> 05:39.636
Good pickings, everyone.

05:40.179 --> 05:42.764
A yen saved is a yen earned.

05:42.890 --> 05:46.435
I think that makes about
five thousand yen.

05:49.063 --> 05:51.398
As long as I have Harvest
by my side,

05:51.482 --> 05:54.526
I'll be set for life.

05:54.902 --> 05:57.237
Hey, looks like that's the user.

05:57.405 --> 05:59.740
He's talking to his Stand…

05:59.907 --> 06:04.036
Yeah… Looks like he's another
product of the bow and arrow.

06:04.120 --> 06:07.832
But it doesn't seem
like he wants to hurt us.

06:17.466 --> 06:18.633
Grin!

06:19.885 --> 06:22.012
You guys…

06:22.221 --> 06:24.806
You can see Harvest?

06:30.146 --> 06:32.648
You really can see it, right?!

06:32.857 --> 06:34.859
Yeah, it's called a Stand.

06:36.610 --> 06:38.486
I'm Josuke Higashikata.

06:38.612 --> 06:40.488
This is Okuyasu Nijimura.

06:41.449 --> 06:45.077
So we're friends!
My first friends!

06:45.953 --> 06:49.706
My name is Shigekiyo Yangu.

06:49.790 --> 06:52.375
I'm an eighth-grader
at Budogaoka Middle School.

06:52.460 --> 06:54.086
I weigh 110 kilograms.

06:54.545 --> 06:58.423
My mommy and daddy
call me "Shigechi."

06:58.507 --> 07:01.218
First it was "Shige-chan,"
then "Shigechi."

07:01.302 --> 07:04.054
I have a pet turtle named Gonta.

07:05.181 --> 07:09.681
The other day, I wanted to see
if the 41 yen, 62 yen,

07:10.102 --> 07:13.396
and 150 yen stamps
tasted different,

07:13.481 --> 07:16.525
so I licked them a lot,
and Mommy yelled at me.

07:16.650 --> 07:19.277
This is a picture of my Mommy.
She yelled at me.

07:19.612 --> 07:20.738
A picture…

07:20.821 --> 07:23.990
Wow, your mom's pretty hot.

07:24.075 --> 07:24.950
Weird.

07:25.034 --> 07:26.410
U-Um…

07:26.911 --> 07:29.371
So, these things are "Harvest"?

07:29.622 --> 07:32.082
Did they really pick up
all these coins?

07:32.249 --> 07:36.002
Yeah. They got 'em from ditches and
the bottom of vending machines…

07:36.253 --> 07:38.129
But I'm not a robber.

07:38.339 --> 07:40.883
The koban policeman said…

07:41.175 --> 07:43.427
"for coin denominations
less than one hundred yen,

07:43.511 --> 07:45.179
no return is necessary."

07:45.262 --> 07:47.722
I hate bad things!

07:47.848 --> 07:50.058
There's nothing bad
about that at all!

07:50.518 --> 07:53.145
In fact, I think
you're doing society a favor.

07:53.270 --> 07:54.396
It's no boatload of cash,

07:54.563 --> 07:55.605
but you're taking forgotten funds

07:55.689 --> 07:58.400
and reinjecting it into
the Japanese economy.

07:58.567 --> 08:00.026
You're doing a great thing.

08:02.530 --> 08:05.741
Really? You think it's great?

08:05.825 --> 08:09.411
Hey, do you think I'm great?

08:10.037 --> 08:12.414
Talk about hidden in plain sight.

08:12.706 --> 08:16.710
No one would ever think of
collecting money like this.

08:17.002 --> 08:20.422
I'm jealous… You're smart.

08:20.589 --> 08:25.089
D-Did you just say I was smart?

08:26.053 --> 08:29.139
N-No one's ever said that
to me before.

08:29.223 --> 08:31.642
I've picked up about
120,000 yen, but…

08:31.725 --> 08:33.601
120,000?!

08:33.894 --> 08:36.813
B-But your words make me
even happier!

08:36.897 --> 08:38.899
A t-total of 120,000?!

08:39.066 --> 08:40.192
Pretty good, right?

08:40.276 --> 08:42.736
J-Just from Morioh?

08:42.820 --> 08:46.824
Yes sir! I never leave Morioh.

08:46.907 --> 08:50.952
I'd get lost and someone
could take me away.

08:51.453 --> 08:55.039
120,000… And I have a measly 12.

08:56.667 --> 08:57.876
Okuyasu…

08:58.460 --> 08:59.878
What's with your left foot?

09:01.797 --> 09:03.465
Whoa, what the…

09:03.549 --> 09:06.718
Who would a thought there'd be
three 50 yen coins over here!

09:06.802 --> 09:09.679
Could they belong to Shigekiyo?

09:09.763 --> 09:11.431
I didn't even see them…

09:11.557 --> 09:13.016
Sneaky bastard…

09:14.768 --> 09:17.729
Here, I'll give you guys half.

09:18.063 --> 09:18.813
Huh?!

09:18.898 --> 09:22.693
We're friends, right?
We can do the same kind of stuff.

09:22.776 --> 09:24.569
R-Really?!

09:24.695 --> 09:26.154
Lucky us!

09:27.364 --> 09:29.532
N-No… Wait.

09:29.617 --> 09:33.829
Look, you can't just simply
hand over money and stuff.

09:33.954 --> 09:36.331
Okay, then I'll put some
real effort into it.

09:37.833 --> 09:41.169
It's all yours.
We're friends, right?

09:41.253 --> 09:43.838
Hey, why are you
making your face all strained?

09:44.006 --> 09:45.132
H-Hey…

09:46.050 --> 09:49.553
Excuse us for a moment while
we have a quick chat, Shigechi.

09:50.638 --> 09:54.183
Listen, Josuke!
Enough of the do-gooder shit, okay?

09:54.266 --> 09:57.686
If he wants to give us the money,
then we take it, dumb-ass!

09:57.770 --> 10:01.982
My pride won't let me do that.
Not this man.

10:02.066 --> 10:04.026
As long as it's not some disease,

10:04.109 --> 10:06.486
I'll take whatever damned thing
someone wants to give me! Got it?!

10:06.612 --> 10:09.406
Take a chill pill!
I getcha, I getcha!

10:09.490 --> 10:10.240
Stop crying!

10:10.324 --> 10:10.991
But…

10:11.075 --> 10:14.745
I am pretty strapped for cash, too.

10:15.037 --> 10:17.414
Which is why I just thought of
a nice little idea

10:17.498 --> 10:19.374
that'll make everyone happy.

10:19.875 --> 10:23.336
Huh? An idea that'll make
everyone happy?

10:24.296 --> 10:26.047
You just leave it to me.

10:31.887 --> 10:34.431
HARVEST

10:34.515 --> 10:39.015
THE PARK IS FOR POLITE CHILDREN
WHO GET ALONG WITH OTHERS
MORIOH CITY

10:34.974 --> 10:39.019
Hey, Shigekiyo.
Can I call you "Shigechi"?

10:39.311 --> 10:40.270
Sure.

10:40.646 --> 10:42.606
Shigechi, we can't
accept your money.

10:42.940 --> 10:44.691
What you were trying to do just now

10:45.025 --> 10:47.944
is no different from trying to
buy your way into friendship.

10:48.195 --> 10:50.739
Huh? B-But I wasn't
trying to do that!

10:50.823 --> 10:55.323
If you ask me,
friendship is something you build.

10:55.536 --> 10:57.829
All I wanted was to…

10:58.038 --> 11:00.749
I know. And I know how you feel.

11:01.125 --> 11:02.835
We Stand users are a team.

11:04.378 --> 11:05.253
And so…

11:05.546 --> 11:10.008
Why don't we build our friendship
with a little business?

11:11.552 --> 11:12.928
Business?

11:13.095 --> 11:16.098
Yeah. Us three putting our heads
together to make a little dough.

11:16.223 --> 11:17.140
You mean this?

11:17.224 --> 11:18.683
No "dough," not "elbow."

11:19.059 --> 11:20.143
What I mean is,

11:20.227 --> 11:23.605
there's only so much money you can
make by picking up leftover change.

11:24.064 --> 11:28.564
I have a more lucrative approach
in mind for Harvest.

11:29.153 --> 11:29.903
Huh?

11:30.738 --> 11:34.533
You have a better idea
than picking up change?

11:34.616 --> 11:36.075
Nothing corrupt about it,

11:36.160 --> 11:38.036
and it won't inconvenience
a single soul.

11:39.246 --> 11:41.665
What kind of idea?

11:41.749 --> 11:44.042
That's where the business part
comes in!

11:44.251 --> 11:45.669
For coming up with the idea,

11:45.753 --> 11:48.714
you can give Okuyasu and me
half of the profits.

11:48.881 --> 11:50.757
The other half goes to you,
Shigechi.

11:50.841 --> 11:54.094
The three of us are going to work
together and pull this thing off.

11:54.261 --> 11:57.222
It'll be a win-win for all of us.

11:57.431 --> 12:01.931
O-Okay! So what do I get to do?

12:02.895 --> 12:04.479
You know what this is, right?

12:03.103 --> 12:06.898
KAMEYU

12:04.730 --> 12:06.648
A b-blue stamp!

12:07.107 --> 12:07.941
You got it!

12:08.025 --> 12:12.362
That sticker you get with every
100 yen purchase from Kameyu,

12:12.446 --> 12:15.073
one of eastern Japan's
biggest department stores.

12:15.282 --> 12:17.242
And I'm pretty sure there are

12:17.409 --> 12:19.119
a bunch of people
who just toss 'em.

12:20.329 --> 12:21.830
Then there's these.

12:21.914 --> 12:23.707
PRODUCT VOUCHER
20 YEN
MEIWADO STATIONERY

12:21.955 --> 12:23.728
A 20-yen voucher from
Meiwado, that stationary store.

12:23.791 --> 12:27.503
OSCAR

12:25.751 --> 12:27.335
A voucher from CD Shop Oscar,

12:27.461 --> 12:27.524
ten will get you
2,000 yen worth of merchandise.

12:27.586 --> 12:29.462
NAGASAKI CLEANERS

12:29.546 --> 12:31.673
YOTSUBA ELECTRONICS

12:30.547 --> 12:31.694
The cleaners,
Märchen Kids toy store…

12:31.757 --> 12:35.927
SERVICE CARD

12:33.592 --> 12:35.885
and this is a card from
Yotsuba Electronics.

12:36.303 --> 12:38.346
Now, this is the important part.

12:38.764 --> 12:43.264
With some, like at Kameyu,
you can get cash back.

12:43.894 --> 12:47.689
Ah, you mean… I got it, Josuke!

12:47.940 --> 12:50.692
I see what you're getting at!

12:52.820 --> 12:56.073
Everyone, it's time!

12:56.073 --> 12:57.449
RUMBLE

12:59.618 --> 13:02.704
One or two might be
worthless scraps of paper…

13:02.788 --> 13:05.999
But picking up
the tens of thousands

13:06.083 --> 13:10.583
of ones lying around town
with Harvest…

13:10.796 --> 13:12.172
Got it.

13:12.339 --> 13:13.965
This trash can!

13:14.633 --> 13:16.134
Now that one!

13:16.218 --> 13:18.803
Got it. Got it.

13:18.887 --> 13:20.138
Got it.

13:20.222 --> 13:23.600
Got it. Got it. Got it.

13:26.603 --> 13:29.480
Th-They just keep piling up!

13:30.524 --> 13:33.693
Your Stand's amazing!
Amazing, Shigechi!

13:35.279 --> 13:36.571
Wow, another compliment.

13:36.697 --> 13:39.783
I'll fix the torn ones
with Shining Diamond.

13:39.867 --> 13:43.203
Yes! We must have
thousands of them now.

13:43.287 --> 13:44.955
No, we must have over 100,000.

13:45.289 --> 13:46.206
Yes!

13:45.706 --> 13:50.206
GRAB

13:46.665 --> 13:48.917
To the unbeatable trio!

13:49.084 --> 13:50.627
Let's go cash in!

13:52.004 --> 13:55.424
But, Josuke,
you sure are a smooth talker.

13:55.674 --> 13:58.093
Pride my ass…

13:58.343 --> 14:01.596
Everyone's gonna be happy.
It's all good.

14:02.222 --> 14:06.392
F-Friendship is neat…

14:10.439 --> 14:14.939
O-Okuyasu, J-Josuke,
will it be okay?

14:16.069 --> 14:18.988
You can turn them into money
that easily?

14:19.072 --> 14:22.617
Relax, Shigechi.
Give Josuke a chance.

14:27.122 --> 14:29.374
It's Okuyasu and…

14:30.000 --> 14:31.042
Who is that?

14:31.919 --> 14:32.920
Okuyasu—

14:53.357 --> 14:55.817
Josuke! H-How'd it go?

14:55.901 --> 14:57.569
Did you get our money?

14:58.737 --> 15:00.739
Did they tell you to piss off?

15:01.323 --> 15:04.617
The CD shop and toy store
don't do cash back.

15:05.118 --> 15:07.036
But we can exchange the coupons

15:07.120 --> 15:10.039
for about 40,000 yen worth of
CDs and video games.

15:10.123 --> 15:11.916
Forget about that!

15:12.084 --> 15:13.543
What about Kameyu?

15:13.627 --> 15:16.379
Didja get cash for
the Kameyu stickers?

15:16.588 --> 15:20.758
Well, something kind of
unexpected happened.

15:21.134 --> 15:23.261
S-Something unexpected?

15:27.683 --> 15:31.520
It unexpectedly
turned into 61,500 yen!

15:32.229 --> 15:34.898
Behold!
The genuine article, Shigechi!

15:35.732 --> 15:38.192
I-It's real!

15:38.277 --> 15:42.364
Real cash right before my eyes!
It's like a dream!

15:42.823 --> 15:44.449
Amazeballs, Shigechi!

15:44.700 --> 15:48.787
Your Stand, Harvest,
is totally amazing!

15:49.162 --> 15:52.290
Y-You really think it's amazing?

15:52.499 --> 15:56.999
Hey… Nobody ever
really compliments me…

15:57.546 --> 15:59.381
Do you really think I'm amazing?

15:59.464 --> 16:02.091
Hey, have a little more confidence,
Shigechi.

16:02.259 --> 16:05.053
You can do something
no one else can.

16:05.387 --> 16:08.348
Okuyasu… Josuke…

16:08.724 --> 16:09.558
All right.

16:09.850 --> 16:11.101
Hey, doll face.

16:11.184 --> 16:12.602
I got a wad of greenbacks
just waiting to be spent!

16:12.686 --> 16:14.062
Wanna have some fun?

16:14.146 --> 16:15.397
Hey, hey, hey, hey!

16:22.279 --> 16:26.779
Oh, yeah. Here, Josuke, Okuyasu.
Here's your share, 10,000 yen.

16:34.541 --> 16:37.252
Shigechi, what is this?

16:39.713 --> 16:44.213
We're comrades… Friends, right?

16:44.926 --> 16:46.594
Yeah, we're a team.

16:47.095 --> 16:50.932
And that's a token
of our friendship.

16:52.559 --> 16:53.643
Hey, wait…

16:53.894 --> 16:56.271
This isn't what we agreed,
Shigechi.

16:56.563 --> 17:00.108
You said half would go to us.

17:00.275 --> 17:04.654
Half of 61,500 yen is 30,750.

17:04.780 --> 17:08.450
R-Really? Did I say that?

17:08.575 --> 17:09.158
What?

17:09.242 --> 17:11.077
Besides…

17:11.161 --> 17:15.661
It w-was my H-Harvest
that did all the collecting.

17:15.791 --> 17:17.334
I did it all!

17:17.417 --> 17:21.045
Y-You guys are all talk
and no action.

17:21.129 --> 17:24.674
Well if Josuke hadn't come up
with the idea,

17:24.758 --> 17:28.011
you would've never thought of
picking up those stupid tickets!

17:28.095 --> 17:30.388
Eventually I would have!

17:30.472 --> 17:32.432
I'm amazing, remember?!

17:32.516 --> 17:34.768
Wrong… No way that cantaloupe
of a noggin

17:34.851 --> 17:36.936
would've ever thought of
something like that!

17:38.605 --> 17:42.942
Hey, stop, Okuyasu.
Easy there, big guy.

17:44.277 --> 17:46.445
This is just great.

17:46.863 --> 17:48.781
He was happy to give us
a few thousand,

17:48.949 --> 17:53.449
but suddenly handing over a few
ten thousands is crossing the line.

17:55.831 --> 18:00.001
He doesn't mean any harm,
but he's got the mind of a kid.

18:00.335 --> 18:01.377
No matter what we say,

18:01.461 --> 18:03.504
it's gonna feel like
we tricked him.

18:04.131 --> 18:07.342
We should be the adults here
and call it a day.

18:07.843 --> 18:11.012
We got 10,000 yen out of it,
and that's good enough.

18:11.680 --> 18:14.974
Well, I guess if you
put it like that…

18:15.058 --> 18:17.894
But he really rubs me
the wrong way!

18:17.978 --> 18:19.980
You sure he's not pulling
a fast one on us?

18:20.063 --> 18:23.399
No, Okuyasu, fighting's not gonna
get us anywhere now.

18:23.650 --> 18:25.276
We just need to school Shigechi

18:25.360 --> 18:27.987
on what a contract between
mature adults really means.

18:28.071 --> 18:30.948
To put a little more jingle
in your pocket?

18:31.074 --> 18:33.159
You fickle bastard…

18:34.327 --> 18:36.662
And that's what I love about you.

18:37.205 --> 18:40.291
All right, we'll gladly take this.

18:41.835 --> 18:43.169
Okuyasu.

18:43.378 --> 18:44.837
Are you thirsty?

18:45.088 --> 18:47.840
Anything you want to drink?
I'll buy.

18:48.049 --> 18:49.717
You're gonna treat me?

18:49.801 --> 18:52.553
Then… make it a Calpis Water.

18:52.721 --> 18:54.097
Then drink some.

18:57.851 --> 19:00.270
Ah! Hey! Why are you
throwing those away?

19:00.353 --> 19:04.148
They're just worthless junk,
like year-end lottery tickets.

19:04.399 --> 19:08.736
I told Shigechi to pick them up
with the other tickets.

19:08.945 --> 19:11.489
You mean these losing New Year's
postcard lottery letters?

19:12.240 --> 19:14.742
How do you know
they're losing tickets?

19:15.035 --> 19:18.872
No one throw's away
a winning ticket, dumb-ass.

19:19.039 --> 19:22.459
Hey, plenty of people forget to
check their numbers

19:22.542 --> 19:24.502
and miss out on
claiming their prizes!

19:24.711 --> 19:27.255
If this wins,
I'm gonna take half of it.

19:27.380 --> 19:29.173
Now promise me, dammit.

19:29.257 --> 19:31.759
Fine. Half it is.

19:32.010 --> 19:35.763
But if you win a sheet of stamps,
you can have it.

19:36.139 --> 19:40.639
EXCITING
WINNING NUMBERS

19:36.973 --> 19:41.102
You really like those cheap
little gambling games, dontcha?

19:41.520 --> 19:41.707
No good… How 'bout this…

19:45.023 --> 19:46.983
I wonder if I can collect

19:47.067 --> 19:50.612
lottery prizes if
I'm still in high school.

19:50.987 --> 19:51.946
Lottery?

19:52.322 --> 19:55.742
As long as you have your ID
and name stamp, it should be fine.

19:56.952 --> 20:00.455
SG GROUP
PAYOUT PERIOD
FROM 1/20/1999
TO 6/21/1999

20:00.747 --> 20:03.291
Nope, another dud.

20:03.750 --> 20:06.127
I thought I had a chance, but…

20:09.089 --> 20:09.839
Hm?

20:10.131 --> 20:11.632
3RD
SG GROUP
BT GROUP

20:11.925 --> 20:16.425
SG Group 121314… Um…

20:18.849 --> 20:22.811
Hey, um if,
if by any chance I won…

20:22.936 --> 20:24.479
Would I have to take it
to the police?

20:24.938 --> 20:27.482
You idiot.
Why would you turn it in to them?

20:27.607 --> 20:30.693
Harvest picked up
only what people threw away.

20:31.152 --> 20:35.281
Worry about winning first,
okay, big man?

20:35.782 --> 20:37.074
Best of luck.

20:37.158 --> 20:41.658
What? SG Group 121314?!

20:42.706 --> 20:45.834
SG GROUP
PAYOUT PERIOD
FROM 1/20/1999
TO 6/21/1999

20:43.123 --> 20:45.855
SG Group 121314?!

20:45.917 --> 20:49.128
WINNING NUMBERS
LIST

20:46.126 --> 20:49.150
SG Group 121314!

20:49.421 --> 20:51.673
Hey, what are you roaring about?

20:51.590 --> 20:53.592
PRIZE 5 MILLION YEN

20:54.301 --> 20:56.845
5 MILLION YEN

20:55.218 --> 20:56.866
5,000,000!

20:57.679 --> 20:59.972
There's no question! I won!

21:01.308 --> 21:04.394
What?! This better not
be some stupid-ass joke!

21:04.311 --> 21:05.145
5 MILLION YEN

21:11.151 --> 21:13.862
Yes! It's a dream come true!

21:14.154 --> 21:16.906
No one in the world has ever
experienced something like this!

21:16.990 --> 21:18.324
Wait, wait, wait, wait!

21:19.117 --> 21:20.576
Settle down, Okuyasu.

21:21.161 --> 21:23.371
Let's just double check
to make sure.

21:23.496 --> 21:27.541
SG Group 121314,
prize 5,000,000 yen.

21:27.709 --> 21:28.543
It's undeniable!

21:28.710 --> 21:30.545
It's seems too good to be true,
but it isn't!

21:31.046 --> 21:33.381
Some old, discarded lottery ticket,

21:33.465 --> 21:35.300
bound for the incinerator.

21:35.717 --> 21:37.468
It expires in a few days.

21:37.677 --> 21:40.971
If they try to ask us a bunch
of pesky questions at the bank,

21:41.097 --> 21:44.350
we say we bought it
fair and square!

21:44.976 --> 21:45.935
Got it?

21:46.353 --> 21:49.022
You bet I do!

21:49.105 --> 21:52.358
Which means
it's our 5,000,000 yen!

21:53.026 --> 21:54.485
Now what should I buy…

21:54.611 --> 21:56.988
First, I'm gonna buy
me some sick Italian shoes!

21:57.113 --> 22:00.741
Then a designer suit
that complements my sleek lines.

22:00.909 --> 22:03.828
Then it's on to Tonio's for
the most expensive food he's got!

22:04.204 --> 22:06.456
And I've gotta take
a trip overseas!

22:06.998 --> 22:08.416
Mine goes in savings!

22:08.959 --> 22:10.794
Live your own sucky life!

22:16.257 --> 22:19.593
<i>My Harvest did all the work…</i>

22:19.719 --> 22:20.761
<i>Five million…</i>

22:20.845 --> 22:24.598
<i>Th-That money stays with me…
all of it.</i>

23:39.132 --> 23:42.009
EPISODE 19
SHIGECHI'S HARVEST, PART 2
